        ('Tech Hunters', 'Wants to keep one decent weapon, one spare repair item, and enough supplies to get through a bad week with Tech Hunters. Would like to get better at a routine task that earns quiet respect instead of attention. Also hopes to keep one reliable ally nearby, even if that only means someone who will not sell them out cheaply.', ''),
        ('Tech Hunters', 'Hopes to make themselves useful enough inside Tech Hunters that people ask for help before they start giving orders. Would like to get better at a routine task that earns quiet respect instead of attention. Also hopes to keep one reliable ally nearby, even if that only means someone who will not sell them out cheaply.', ''),
        ('The Gorrillo Bandits', 'Find a decent pair of boots before the next long march across the burning sands. Earn enough scraps from the next ambush to afford a proper meal at the waypoint camp.', ''),
        ('The Gorrillo Bandits', 'Keep the campfire hidden from patrols tonight without choking everyone on smoke. Memorize the location of that clean waterhole the boss mentioned last week.', ''),
        ('The Gorrillo Bandits', 'Sharpen the rusted blade taken from that last traveler before it snaps mid-fight. Convince one of the newer recruits to trade their almost-intact shirt for a few extra ration shares.', ''),
        ('The Gorrillo Bandits', 'Avoid getting assigned to the forward scouting group again since those positions always take the worst hits. Stockpile a small personal reserve of food where the others won''t find it.', ''),
        ('The Gorrillo Bandits', 'Practice the heavy swing the war-chief showed until shoulders stop aching halfway through. Find a replacement for the cracked club before the next raid is called.', ''),
        ('The Gorrillo Bandits', 'Convince the others to move camp somewhere with better cover from the wind. Mend the tears in the sleeping roll before the cold nights return.', ''),
        ('The Gorrillo Bandits', 'Prove reliable enough to be trusted with carrying a share of the group''s meager copper stash. Learn which direction the local slave patrols ride at dusk so those roads can be avoided.', ''),
        ('The Gorrillo Bandits', 'Trade the extra leather scrap to the fixer at the outpost for a working canteen. Keep head down during the next argument over loot splits and avoid drawing the boss''s temper.', ''),
        ('The Gorrillo Bandits', 'Memorize the patrol schedules along the eastern trade road to pick safer crossing points. Find a shaded spot to stash gear during the midday heat where the wild dogs won''t sniff it out.', ''),
        ('The Gorrillo Bandits', 'Get on the good side of the fighter who shares the night watch by offering a portion of dried meat. Figure out which of the younger bandits can actually be trusted to watch a flank during a fight.', ''),
        ('The Gorrillo Bandits', 'Convince the camp cook to boil the water from the new stream before the sickening runs through camp again. Repair the worn strap on the backpack before it fails completely on a long haul.', ''),
        ('The Gorrillo Bandits', 'Claim a spot near the fire pit that isn''t right where the smoke blows every evening. Gather enough dry brush before nightfall to keep the embers going until dawn.', ''),
        ('The Gorrillo Bandits', 'Wants to keep a little extra food and clean bandages set aside so life inside The Gorrillo Bandits feels less precarious. Would like to get better at a routine task that earns quiet respect instead of attention. Also hopes to keep one reliable ally nearby, even if that only means someone who will not sell them out cheaply.', ''),
        ('The Gorrillo Bandits', 'Hopes to hold onto a slightly safer sleeping spot and stop being pushed aside so easily within The Gorrillo Bandits. Would like to get better at a routine task that earns quiet respect instead of attention. Also hopes to keep one reliable ally nearby, even if that only means someone who will not sell them out cheaply.', ''),
        ('The Gorrillo Bandits', 'Wants to keep one decent weapon, one spare repair item, and enough supplies to get through a bad week with The Gorrillo Bandits. Would like to get better at a routine task that earns quiet respect instead of attention. Also hopes to keep one reliable ally nearby, even if that only means someone who will not sell them out cheaply.', ''),
        ('The Holy Nation', 'He needs to find a reliable source of iron plates to repair the dents in his holy armor before the next inspection. Earning a nod of approval from the High Paladin would secure his standing in the barracks for another season.', 'male'),
        ('The Holy Nation', 'His wheat plot is showing signs of blight, and he must consult the other farmers about a crop rotation fix before it spreads. He also hopes to finish memorizing the evening prayers so he can lead the household in worship without stumbling over the verses.', 'male'),
        ('The Holy Nation', 'He wants to trade a few spare cattan for a second-standard sword so he is not caught patrolling with only a rusty blade. Keeping his boots resoled before the rainy season hits is another small chore he keeps putting off.', 'male'),
        ('The Holy Nation', 'He has been assigned to watch the eastern approach for a fortnight and intends to log every traveler without mistake to prove his reliability. Saving enough cats to buy a proper bedroll would make those cold overnight shifts far more bearable.', 'male'),
        ('The Holy Nation', 'He hopes to earn a transfer from the fields to the temple guard by volunteering for every extra shift the sergeants post. He also wants to mend the gap in the wall behind his quarters before his wife complains to the district overseer.', 'male'),
        ('The Holy Nation', 'He is tasked with inspecting the outlying farms for unregistered skeletons and plans to cover the southern loop before midweek. He keeps meaning to ask the senior paladin about a persistent ache in his sword shoulder that flares after long marches.', 'male'),
        ('The Holy Nation', 'He wants to forge a standard longsword good enough that the armory accepts it for issue rather than selling it to a scrap merchant. Paying off his debt at the grain store would finally let him sleep without dreading the collector.', 'male'),
        ('The Holy Nation', 'She must prove her usefulness to her husband''s household before the elder women find fault with her work. A second set of prayer candles would help her keep up appearances during evening devotions without borrowing from neighbors.', 'female'),
        ('The Holy Nation', 'She needs to set aside enough grain before winter to keep her children fed without asking for charity. Finding a suitable match for her eldest daughter would secure the girl''s future and ease her own mind.', 'female'),
        ('The Holy Nation', 'Since her husband passed she has relied on his brother''s protection but she wants to save enough cots to rent her own small room. A warm shawl would make the long hours of mending more bearable through the cold season.', 'female'),
        ('The Holy Nation', 'She hopes to finish enough woven cloth this week to trade for a new cooking pot. Keeping her children quiet during services is the only way to avoid the disapproving stares from the priest''s wife.', 'female'),
        ('The Holy Nation', 'She wants to learn which market sellers will extend credit without reporting her to the Okranite guards. Earning a few extra cats by washing clothes for the soldiers'' families would let her buy proper shoes before the rains come.', 'female'),
        ('The Holy Nation', 'She must ensure her son memorizes his Okranite verses before his next evaluation at the temple. Keeping the kitchen stocked with salted fish requires careful management of the household budget her husband allows her.', 'female'),
        ('The Holy Nation', 'She prays her husband''s temper stays mild so she can avoid the marks that draw pity from the other women. A small herb garden behind the shed would give her something of her own to tend without drawing suspicion.', 'female'),
        ('The Holy Nation', 'She needs to repair the roof patch before the rainy season tests the leak again. Trading a few extra vegetables at market would finally let her replace the worn blanket on her bed.', 'female'),
        ('Traders Guild', 'Needs to replace a worn caravan backpack before the next long haul to Sho-Battai. Also wants to set aside enough cats this season to afford a better weapon than this rusty sabre.', ''),
        ('Traders Guild', 'Hopes to earn a recommendation from the outpost supervisor by keeping the inventory ledgers spotless. Keeps putting off repairing the leaky roof of the sleeping quarters, but knows it needs doing before the rains come.', ''),
        ('Traders Guild', 'Worries about the pack beasts coming down with gut parasites again and wants to stock up on medicinal herbs before the next caravan moves out. Just wants a single night of decent sleep without waking to check on the goods.', ''),
        ('Traders Guild', 'Trying to prove reliable enough to be assigned guard duty on the lucrative Stack routes instead of the boring local patrols. Also needs to find a cobbler who will patch these boots for a fair price instead of trying to upsell.', ''),
        ('Traders Guild', 'Desperate to pay off the outstanding debt for that spoiled batch of rum before the guild deducts it from next season''s advance. Secretly practicing swinging a jitte in the evenings so the veterans stop calling them useless in a fight.', ''),
        ('Traders Guild', 'Wants to negotiate a steady supply contract with the Holy Farm growers rather than buying at spot prices each week. Has been sleeping poorly on the hard counter mats and just wants enough saved for a proper cot.', ''),
        ('Traders Guild', 'Trying to learn which border checkpoints can be bribed cheaply to avoid the full inspection delays, since faster trips mean better margins. Needs to replace the stolen skimmer backpack with something affordable before the next run.', ''),
        ('Traders Guild', 'Keeps getting assigned to the same dull route through the Border Zone and wants a transfer to something with better opportunity for tips. Has been eating nothing but dustwiches for weeks and craves a proper meal at a Waystation inn.', ''),
        ('Traders Guild', 'Concerned that the newer recruits are too green to spot an ambush and plans to run practice drills on the next rest stop. Still trying to collect the unpaid bounty voucher from the last trip through Okran''s Valley.', ''),
        ('Traders Guild', 'Hopes to finally afford a mercenary escort contract instead of relying on the guild''s stretched-thin guards. Wonders if investing in a crossbow would be smarter than continuing to pay for hired muscle.', ''),
        ('Traders Guild', 'Wants to earn enough trust from the senior traders to be allowed to handle rare weapons trades instead of just bulk rice and copper. Has been nursing a sore shoulder from hauling crates and hopes it heals before the next loading day.', ''),
        ('Traders Guild', 'Trying to build a reputation for never shorting a customer on weight so that settlements request them by name for deliveries. Keeps meaning to mend the holes in the winter coat before the temperature drops further in the highlands.', ''),
        ('Traders Guild', 'Wants to keep a little extra food and clean bandages set aside so life inside Traders Guild feels less precarious. Would like to get better at a routine task that earns quiet respect instead of attention. Also hopes to keep one reliable ally nearby, even if that only means someone who will not sell them out cheaply.', ''),
        ('Traders Guild', 'Hopes to hold onto a slightly safer sleeping spot and stop being pushed aside so easily within Traders Guild. Would like to get better at a routine task that earns quiet respect instead of attention. Also hopes to keep one reliable ally nearby, even if that only means someone who will not sell them out cheaply.', ''),
        ('Traders Guild', 'Wants to keep one decent weapon, one spare repair item, and enough supplies to get through a bad week with Traders Guild. Would like to get better at a routine task that earns quiet respect instead of attention. Also hopes to keep one reliable ally nearby, even if that only means someone who will not sell them out cheaply.', ''),
        ('United Cities', 'Save enough cats to commission a proper steel blade from the weapon smith in Sho-Battai. The issued iron katana keeps chipping during patrol drills and I refuse to be embarrassed again.', ''),
        ('United Cities', 'Find a reliable supplier of rice for the warehouse district before the caravan season begins. My supervisor noticed the shortfall last month and I cannot afford another mark on my record.', ''),
        ('United Cities', 'Earn enough extra coin tutoring noble children in basic calligraphy to move out of the cramped servant quarters. The damp walls are ruining my scrolls and my health.', ''),
        ('United Cities', 'Get reassigned to the border garrison at Rebirth where the work is steady and the officers actually rotate shifts. These fourteen-hour gate shifts in the city heat are draining me.', ''),
        ('United Cities', 'Secure a trade permit for Heng before the new quarterly fees take effect. The extra paperwork is tedious but the profit margins make it worth the trouble.', ''),
        ('United Cities', 'Practice my stance work every morning until my legs stop shaking during the weekly inspection. Captain Yoshida watches me specifically now and I need to prove I belong in the samurai ranks.', ''),
        ('United Cities', 'Replace my worn sandals before the rainy season turns the roads to mud outside Okran''s Shield. My feet are constantly blistered and the cobbler on Second Street owes me a favor.', ''),
        ('United Cities', 'Bribe the right clerk to get my name on the night watch roster instead of dawn patrol. The early shifts leave me exhausted and I keep nodding off during afternoon drills.', ''),
        ('United Cities', 'Save enough to purchase a second water processor for the shop so I can take on larger orders. One more profitable season and I can finally hire a proper apprentice.', ''),
        ('United Cities', 'Find out which slave is stealing dried meat from the storehouse and put a stop to it. The losses are small but the principle matters if I want to be taken seriously as an overseer.', ''),
        ('United Cities', 'Negotiate a better rate with the grain merchants before winter shipments slow down. My inn cannot survive another season of razor-thin margins on rice porridge.', ''),
        ('United Cities', 'Learn enough basic sword work to pass the militia qualification exam next spring. The extra pay grade would finally let me afford a real bed instead of sleeping in the barracks loft.', ''),
        ('United Cities', 'Wants to keep a little extra food and clean bandages set aside so life inside United Cities feels less precarious. Would like to get better at a routine task that earns quiet respect instead of attention. Also hopes to keep one reliable ally nearby, even if that only means someone who will not sell them out cheaply.', ''),
        ('United Cities', 'Hopes to hold onto a slightly safer sleeping spot and stop being pushed aside so easily within United Cities. Would like to get better at a routine task that earns quiet respect instead of attention. Also hopes to keep one reliable ally nearby, even if that only means someone who will not sell them out cheaply.', ''),
        ('United Cities', 'Wants to keep one decent weapon, one spare repair item, and enough supplies to get through a bad week with United Cities. Would like to get better at a routine task that earns quiet respect instead of attention. Also hopes to keep one reliable ally nearby, even if that only means someone who will not sell them out cheaply.', ''),
        ('United Heroes League', 'Need to sharpen my spare blade before the next patrol rotation. The quartermaster has been glaring at me for returning gear dull. Maybe I can trade some extra ration tickets for a proper whetstone.', ''),
        ('United Heroes League', 'Still trying to memorize the League code of conduct so I stop fumbling during inspections. Senior members keep correcting my salute form. If I can just pass the basic readiness review, I''ll finally get assigned to a real patrol squad.', ''),
        ('United Heroes League', 'My armor padding is wearing thin and chafing something awful on long walks. I should ask the supply clerk if any replacements came in from the last trade run. A few more cogs and I could afford custom fittings from the leather worker in town.', ''),
        ('United Heroes League', 'Worried about my standing after that argument with the squad leader last week. Trying to volunteer for extra supply runs to show I''m still committed. Need to be seen as reliable if I want any chance at the promotion review next season.', ''),
        ('United Heroes League', 'The recruit I''m supposed to be mentoring still can''t land a proper strike. Spent half the morning going over basic stance drills again. At this rate, neither of us will pass the quarterly assessment.', ''),
        ('United Heroes League', 'Running low on medical supplies and the next restock caravan is days away. Bandages I can scrounge, but proper splints are hard to come by. Should check if the herbalist in the market district has anything useful for wound care.', ''),
        ('United Heroes League', 'My bunk mate keeps stealing my footlocker space and it''s driving me mad. Trying to save enough for a private sleeping alcove on the second floor. A few more successful bounties and I can afford the upgrade without borrowing.', ''),
        ('United Heroes League', 'The evening watch rotations keep getting shifted around and it''s ruining my sleep. Trying to trade shifts with someone who prefers dawn patrol. If that doesn''t work, I''ll just have to adjust my training schedule to match the new times.', ''),
        ('United Heroes League', 'Haven''t heard back from my family in Stack and the mail runners are unreliable. Thinking about paying a traveling merchant to carry a letter on their next trip. Just need to know they''re doing alright without me sending cogs back regularly.', ''),
        ('United Heroes League', 'My running stamina is terrible compared to the others in my unit. Started waking up early to do extra laps around the compound before breakfast. The captain noticed my effort yesterday and gave me an approving nod, which felt good.', ''),
        ('United Heroes League', 'The communal meals have been thin lately and I''m always hungry by second watch. Tried bartering some of my salvage finds for extra dried meat from the kitchen staff. Just need to keep my energy up until the supply situation improves.', ''),
        ('United Heroes League', 'Been assigned to archive duty sorting old mission reports and it''s tedious work. Hoping if I organize everything properly, the records keeper will put in a good word for me. Would much rather be out on patrol than dusting old papers and fixing broken bindings.', ''),
        ('United Heroes League', 'Wants to keep a little extra food and clean bandages set aside so life inside United Heroes League feels less precarious. Would like to get better at a routine task that earns quiet respect instead of attention. Also hopes to keep one reliable ally nearby, even if that only means someone who will not sell them out cheaply.', ''),
        ('United Heroes League', 'Hopes to hold onto a slightly safer sleeping spot and stop being pushed aside so easily within United Heroes League. Would like to get better at a routine task that earns quiet respect instead of attention. Also hopes to keep one reliable ally nearby, even if that only means someone who will not sell them out cheaply.', ''),
        ('United Heroes League', 'Wants to keep one decent weapon, one spare repair item, and enough supplies to get through a bad week with United Heroes League. Would like to get better at a routine task that earns quiet respect instead of attention. Also hopes to keep one reliable ally nearby, even if that only means someone who will not sell them out cheaply.', ''),
        ('Western Hive', 'Gather enough cactus to fill the community stores before the next ration distribution. Stay on the good side of the foreman so I get assigned to the shaded work shifts.', ''),
        ('Western Hive', 'Learn which trader pays the most for raw iron so I can bring back better earnings for my unit. Keep my pickaxe sharp and wrapped in cloth so it doesn''t chip on the hard rock veins.', ''),
        ('Western Hive', 'Memorize the patrol route through the eastern canyons until I can walk it without getting lost. Prove I''m reliable enough to be trusted with a weapon of my own instead of borrowing one each shift.', ''),
        ('Western Hive', 'Find a quiet spot near the outpost where I can rest during midday heat without getting shouted at. Save enough tags to trade for a second waterskin so I don''t go thirsty on long foraging runs.', ''),
        ('Western Hive', 'Convince the kitchen workers to give me extra ration portions in exchange for early deliveries. Keep my antennae clean so I can detect sand spiders before they get too close.', ''),
        ('Western Hive', 'Practice wrapping bandages quickly so I can help injured workers without fumbling. Earn enough trust from the elder guides to be allowed on deep desert scavenging trips.', ''),
        ('Western Hive', 'Repair the broken fence section near my sleeping pod before the foreman notices and assigns me penalty labor. Trade my spare copper ore for a decent pair of boots that don''t chafe my legs.', ''),
        ('Western Hive', 'Learn the hand signals the scout party uses so I can understand their warnings during dust storms. Avoid getting assigned to the southern watch post where the wind never stops blowing sand.', ''),
        ('Western Hive', 'Barter with the traveling merchants for a better cutting blade to harvest cactus more efficiently. Make sure my work unit gets credit for the iron we collected instead of letting the next shift claim it.', ''),
        ('Western Hive', 'Keep my assigned storage niche organized so inspectors don''t write me up for clutter. Save a small portion of my food to trade with the mechanic who fixes water pumps.', ''),
        ('Western Hive', 'Get through the entire moon cycle without drawing the queen''s attendants'' attention for any mistakes. Find out which of the neighboring workers can be relied on to cover my duties if I fall ill.', ''),
        ('Western Hive', 'Learn to mend tears in my own wrappings instead of always asking the supply keeper for replacements. Stay on good terms with the hive guard so they don''t assign me to the distant mining shafts.', ''),
        ('Western Hive', 'Wants to keep a little extra food and clean bandages set aside so life inside Western Hive feels less precarious. Would like to get better at a routine task that earns quiet respect instead of attention. Also hopes to keep one reliable ally nearby, even if that only means someone who will not sell them out cheaply.', ''),
        ('Western Hive', 'Hopes to hold onto a slightly safer sleeping spot and stop being pushed aside so easily within Western Hive. Would like to get better at a routine task that earns quiet respect instead of attention. Also hopes to keep one reliable ally nearby, even if that only means someone who will not sell them out cheaply.', ''),
        ('Western Hive', 'Wants to keep one decent weapon, one spare repair item, and enough supplies to get through a bad week with Western Hive. Would like to get better at a routine task that earns quiet respect instead of attention. Also hopes to keep one reliable ally nearby, even if that only means someone who will not sell them out cheaply.', ''),
        ('White Eyebrow Clan', 'Hoping to earn enough cats from bounties to replace the worn wrappings on my fists before the next training cycle. I need to prove I can handle harder contracts without slowing down the seniors.', ''),
        ('White Eyebrow Clan', 'I want to mend the tear in my tunic before the master notices and assigns me extra chores as punishment. Finding a reliable trader who sells decent fabric in this region would save me a lot of grief.', ''),
        ('White Eyebrow Clan', 'My knees ache after long patrols and I worry I will not keep up with the younger members much longer. I just want to finish my route shifts without falling behind and losing face before the clan.', ''),
        ('White Eyebrow Clan', 'I have been tasked with inventorying the dry goods and need to figure out how to make the rice stores last another week. If I can find a cheap grain supplier in the nearby town it would ease everyone''s stress.', ''),
        ('White Eyebrow Clan', 'I am determined to finally land a clean hit on my sparring partner during the next practice session. Keeping my footing on the dusty training ground has been a struggle and I need to fix that.', ''),
        ('White Eyebrow Clan', 'I need to return the favor I owe the scout who shared her rations with me last week during the long watch. Maybe I can take her night shift so she can rest properly for once.', ''),
        ('White Eyebrow Clan', 'I want to learn the footwork patterns the seniors use but nobody seems willing to teach me yet. I figure if I watch closely during morning drills and practice alone I might pick up enough to stop stumbling.', ''),
        ('White Eyebrow Clan', 'Making sure the training dummies stay repaired and bound tight is my responsibility and I keep falling behind. I just need a steady supply of sturdy rope and a few spare planks to stay ahead of the wear.', ''),
        ('White Eyebrow Clan', 'I hope to save enough from my share of the bounty money to buy a proper weapon instead of relying on borrowed gear. It would feel good to own something I can maintain and sharpen myself.', ''),
        ('White Eyebrow Clan', 'I have been trying to get on the good side of the quartermaster so she will assign me better bedding. If I help her sort the incoming supplies she might put in a word for me.', ''),
        ('White Eyebrow Clan', 'I want to be chosen for the next surface supply run instead of staying cooped up inside the walls. Showing the master I can move quietly through hostile territory is the only way I will ever be trusted with real scouting work.', ''),
        ('White Eyebrow Clan', 'The wind comes through the barracks cracks and I keep waking up stiff and sore before dawn drills. I just want to find enough scrap cloth to seal the gaps so I can sleep properly and train well.', ''),
        ('White Eyebrow Clan', 'Wants to keep a little extra food and clean bandages set aside so life inside White Eyebrow Clan feels less precarious. Would like to get better at a routine task that earns quiet respect instead of attention. Also hopes to keep one reliable ally nearby, even if that only means someone who will not sell them out cheaply.', ''),
